('PUBLIC', NULL, '低脂油醋汁', 'Low Fat Vinaigrette With Yogurt or Tomato or Avocado Variations', '["酸奶油醋汁", "Vinaigrette"]', '["加餐"]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '["咸鲜"]', '["快速"]', 'Entered for safe-keeping. From Martha Rose Shulman''s "Fast Vegetarian Feasts", received in February 2009 Cookbook Swap. A little bit of oil can go a long way. Instead of whisking, use a blender to make a fairly thick, emulsified mixture. You can vary this with any herbs or spices you wish (the 2-3 teaspoons of fresh herbs can be any combination you prefer, suggested herbs are listed). The author recommends the yogurt variation when "you want to eat nothing but salads, but have to work in protein." I recommend the Avocado variation during the maintenance phase of WW, because the avocado has healthy fat and aids digestion if your calories permit. See Recipe #361079 #361079 for a tasty broth variation.', '["wine vinegar", "cider vinegar", "garlic clove", "dry mustard", "Dijon mustard", "dried marjoram", "dried basil", "dried tarragon", "fresh parsley", "fresh chives", "fresh ground pepper", "onion", "water", "broth", "Tamari Bouillon Broth With Instant Variation", "plain low-fat yogurt", "tomatoes", "tomato juice", "avocado", "plain low-fat yogurt", "paprika", "ground cumin"]', 8, '1.00', '份', '71.40', '1.80', '5.70', '4.10', 'foodcom_source_value', '1', '["牛奶"]', 'REVIEWED', 'APPROVED', 'foodcom-recipes-and-reviews-v2', '361504', 'v2', NULL, 'NONE', NULL, NOW(), NOW()),
